PE 913: Row-Major vs Column-Major / 行主序vs列主序

=== Problem Overview ===
Row-major index at (i,j):  val_rm = (i-1)*n + j
Column-major index at (i,j): val_cm = (j-1)*n + i

They are equal when (i-1)*n + j = (j-1)*n + i
=> (i-j)(n-1) = 0 => when n=1 or i=j
So diagonal entries always match!

The problem extends this to a counting/weighting scheme
over all n up to some large bound N.

=== Key Concepts ===
  1. Coordinate mapping between row-major and column-major
  2. Solving systems of congruences
  3. Efficient summation over large ranges
  4. Prefix sums of number-theoretic functions

